## erlbutt production node.
##
## Distribution is enabled but bound to the loopback interface, so the node
## is reachable for `bin/ssb remote_console|stop|ping` from the same host
## while NOT accepting distribution connections from other machines.
##
## Set SSB_COOKIE per install and treat it as a secret — the default below is
## a placeholder, and deliberately not a real value, because this file is in
## git.  On a box with a public IP the cookie is the only thing between a
## reachable distribution port and arbitrary code execution.  To take the node
## fully off distribution (no remsh, and bin/ssb stop|ping|remote_console
## stop working — you must then manage the OS process directly), comment out
## the -name and -setcookie lines below.
-name ${SSB_NODE:-ssb@127.0.0.1}
-setcookie ${SSB_COOKIE:-change-me-in-production}

## Bind the distribution listener to loopback only.
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## Pin the distribution listener port.  It is random by default, and a random
## port cannot be forwarded: `ssh -L 9100:localhost:9100` is the only way to
## reach a loopback-bound node from another machine (maxbutt/distel), so an
## unpinned port means the tunnel breaks on every restart.  Setting min alone
## is enough — inet_dist_listen_max defaults to min, pinning it exactly rather
## than opening a range.  Do NOT open this port on the firewall.
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min ${SSB_DIST_PORT:-9100}

+K true
+A 16
